      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This could be really cool, but I'm not too sure how well it could be implemented.  Especially when it's, essentially, only sociologically different than using the \"show very poor\" option.  And given that, there's a large likelihood of abuse; \"Oh no, my avatar is rated Very Poor. I should just check the Spectacle option so people won't block it.\"  \n\nThe only way I can realistically seeing this work is if we had the category + a symbol for it, but hide/show options remained as they are functionally.  Maybe some flavor text in the performance options to inform users as well?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-06-20T06:19:48.595Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's very hard for regular users to determine if an Avatar is meant to be an avatar showing something nice that someone had made, like particle shows and fancy gimmick avatars that the person won't regularly use, or if it's a badly optimized avatar with unnecessary amounts of materials and meshes due to either ignorance or zero effort to optimize.\n\nMaybe a separate category (and options to hide/show) for these kinds of avatars could work? Something like a choice for people to unhide that one particular avatar category if they wanted to see something good, or if it would automatically hide when the world is too crowded? For avatar makers who can't/prefer not to communicate with voice chat to show people their work, this might help a little bit.\n\nThe aim is to differentiate people who want to be \"entertainers\" trying to show their work and people who just want to socialize. I'm aware that some spiteful people might categorize all their avatars as these kinds of avatars if they can't be bothered, but maybe it could be done in a better way.",
